From 5ce8d69104a677f98ebab6319ad5b7e0f44998e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amr Elsaqqa <amrelsaqqa@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:11:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] mt7621: bring-up tracing in the MIPS core

The env-gated MT7621_* instrumentation the machine's bring-up needed, kept out
of the target-wide series because only this machine's guests use it:
MT7621_PCWATCH (translated-block ring in cpu-exec), MT7621_GICLOG /
MT7621_IPILOG (GIC register and IPI tracing), MT7621_GICCLOG (counter
compare/count tracing), MT7621_GICTIMERLOG (timer trace),
MT7621_GICTIMER_LEGACY (pre-fix compare semantics) and the RECVLOG
syscall-return helper the SYSLOG patch extends.
